{"slug":"16-01-two-variable-data-1-2-3","title":"16.01 Two-Variable Data 1, 2 & 3","subject":"ESSENTIALS","total":40,"questions":[{"id":26462,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/TEQXi1PInmMkO2ENxfH8WeTU5wYeL3r506Fos5tN.png\" style=\"width: 197.983px;\"></div><br>Of the following, which is the best model for the data in the scatterplot?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97957,"html":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=2x^2-13x-20</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">13</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span></span></span></span><br></p>","correct":false},{"id":97958,"html":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=2x^2-11x+20</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">11</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span></span></span></span><br></p>","correct":true},{"id":97959,"html":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=2x^2-5x-3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span><br></p>","correct":false},{"id":97960,"html":"<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=2x^2-5x+3</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">y</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8974em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span><br></p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26496,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/0UGiuWsfg3KbEqbVqzI42GCQ3e6GkwLMPbP5MrWC.png\" style=\"width: 369.631px; height: 309.517px;\"></div><br>In an experiment, a heated cup of coffee is removed from a heat source, and the cup of coffee is then left in a room that is kept at a constant temperature. The graph above shows the temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit (0F), of the coffee immediately after being removed from the heat source and at 10-minute intervals thereafter. During which of the following 10-minute intervals does the temperature of the coffee decrease at the greatest average rate?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98035,"html":"<p>Between 0 and 10 minutes</p>","correct":true},{"id":98036,"html":"<p>Between 30 and 40 minutes</p>","correct":false},{"id":98037,"html":"<p>Between 50 and 60 minutes</p>","correct":false},{"id":98038,"html":"<p>Between 90 and 100 minutes</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26497,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/cFWvideZ8aln1yFpOwN1ALZQImhRRm5x89tXqU5r.png\" style=\"width: 258.991px;\"></div><br>The scatterplot above shows the high temperature on a certain day and the elevation of 8 different locations in the Lake Tahoe Basin. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. What temperature is predicted by the line of best fit for a location in the Lake Tahoe Basin with an elevation of 8,500 feet?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98039,"html":"<p>37<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>F</p>","correct":false},{"id":98040,"html":"<p>39<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></semantics></math></span></span>F</p>","correct":true},{"id":98041,"html":"<p>41<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></semantics></math></span></span>F</p>","correct":false},{"id":98042,"html":"<p>43<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></semantics></math></span></span>F</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26498,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/XYP6MTzfUdSI3T5C0KtdXRN586KLMhVrY8iZot73.png\" style=\"width: 302.983px;\"></div><br><p></p><p>The line graph shows the number of graduates from the classes of 2001 through 2007 at a certain school who enrolled in college within 24 months of graduation. Of the following, which class had the fewest graduates who enrolled in college within 24 months of graduation?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98043,"html":"<p>2002</p>","correct":true},{"id":98044,"html":"<p>2004</p>","correct":false},{"id":98045,"html":"<p>2005</p>","correct":false},{"id":98046,"html":"<p>2007</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26499,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/34ISZLDV47UCSnKCVIbamolQOa6mXxVflnKekynh.png\" style=\"width: 304.972px;\"></div><br>Theresa ran on a treadmill for thirty minutes, and her time and speed are shown on the graph above. According to the graph, which of the following statements is NOT true concerning Theresa’s run?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98047,"html":"<p>Theresa ran at a constant speed for five minutes.</p>","correct":false},{"id":98048,"html":"<p>Theresa’s speed was increasing for a longer period of time than it was decreasing.</p>","correct":true},{"id":98049,"html":"<p>Theresa’s speed decreased at a constant rate during the last five minutes.</p>","correct":false},{"id":98050,"html":"<p>Theresa’s speed reached its maximum during the last ten minutes.</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26500,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/qp7p3lBLhF1KTq8hmAicZzE9Kbqemmb3pTLMnPfO.png\" style=\"width: 290.98px;\"></div><br>The densities of different concentrations of grape juice are shown in the scatterplot above. According to the trend shown by the data, which of the following is closest to the predicted density, in kilograms per cubic meter (kg/m3), for grape juice with a concentration of 60%?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98051,"html":"<p>1,200</p>","correct":false},{"id":98052,"html":"<p>1,250</p>","correct":false},{"id":98053,"html":"<p>1,300</p>","correct":true},{"id":98054,"html":"<p>1,350</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26501,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/xgG0GRKSugszyAIOBsOF1LWCDm4zNwJExQqwXqCy.png\" style=\"width: 343.991px;\"></div><br>According to the line graph above, between which two consecutive years was there the greatest change in the number of 3.D movies released?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98055,"html":"<p>2003-2004</p>","correct":false},{"id":98056,"html":"<p>2008-2009</p>","correct":false},{"id":98057,"html":"<p>2009-2010</p>","correct":false},{"id":98058,"html":"<p>2010-2011</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26502,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/4XZiRQZXbb38vc6Qag5sebnT9si4laIg1e2A2HHo.png\" style=\"width: 207.983px;\"></div><br>Which of the following could be an equation for a line of best fit for the data in the scatterplot?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98059,"html":"<p>y = -x + 6</p>","correct":true},{"id":98060,"html":"<p>y = -x - 6</p>","correct":false},{"id":98061,"html":"<p>y = 6x + 1</p>","correct":false},{"id":98062,"html":"<p>y = 6x - 1</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26503,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/jg0HNipwCJLjvInDW3BwQ913sRqV1FaNZKoUoUdh.png\" style=\"width: 310.625px; height: 269.697px;\"></div><br><p></p><p>The graph above shows the relationship between the speed of a particular car, in miles per hour, and its corresponding braking distance, in feet. Approximately how many feet greater will the car’s braking distance be when the car is traveling at 50 miles per hour than when the car is traveling at 30 miles per hour?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98063,"html":"<p>75</p>","correct":false},{"id":98064,"html":"<p>125</p>","correct":true},{"id":98065,"html":"<p>175</p>","correct":false},{"id":98066,"html":"<p>250</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26504,"html":"<p>The scatterplot shows the temperature y, in 0F, recorded by a meteorologist at various times x, in days since June 1.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/JoizMZL64hjRedV7LGIffv60v5wkJ03MJEqSBVEe.png\" style=\"width: 347.071px; height: 324.946px;\"></div><br>During which of the following time periods did the greatest increase in recorded temperature take place?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98067,"html":"<p>From x = 6 to x = 7</p>","correct":false},{"id":98068,"html":"<p>From x = 5 to x = 6</p>","correct":false},{"id":98069,"html":"<p>From x = 2 to x = 3</p>","correct":true},{"id":98070,"html":"<p>From x = 1 to x = 2</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26505,"html":"<p>A study was done to determine a new car’s stopping distance when it was traveling at different speeds. The study was done on a dry road with good surface conditions. The results are shown below, along with the graph of a quadratic function that models the data.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/p2RP6WdUM6XXwgqvev3Qu5CF0GSYFirvYGyeD9PK.png\" style=\"width: 271.119px; height: 251.374px;\"><br></div><br>According to the model, which of the following is the best estimate for the stopping distance, in feet, if the vehicle was traveling 55 miles per hour?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98071,"html":"<p>25</p>","correct":false},{"id":98072,"html":"<p>30</p>","correct":false},{"id":98073,"html":"<p>210</p>","correct":true},{"id":98074,"html":"<p>250</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26506,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/tEVLjJPgRINIM8rGRjVboGyyyGQwn87oMhwfNijy.png\" style=\"width: 259.986px;\"></div><br>The scatterplot above shows the high temperature on a certain day and the elevation of 8 different locations in the Lake Tahoe Basin. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. Which of the following statements best describes the association between the elevation and the temperature of locations in the Lake Tahoe Basin?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98075,"html":"<p>As the elevation increases, the temperature tends to increase.</p>","correct":false},{"id":98076,"html":"<p>As the elevation increases, the temperature tends to decrease.</p>","correct":true},{"id":98077,"html":"<p>As the elevation decreases, the temperature tends to decrease.</p>","correct":false},{"id":98078,"html":"<p>There is no association between the elevation and the temperature.</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26507,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/efaUiMrEFyDrr8UxC8mCftYtaTIb7wDFGwuy3S2f.png\" style=\"width: 300.98px;\"></div><br><p></p><p>The scatterplot above shows the densities of 7 planetoids, in grams per cubic centimeter, with respect to their average distances from the Sun in astronomical units (AU). The line of best fit is also shown. An astronomer has discovered a new planetoid about 1.2 AU from the Sun. According to the line of best fit, which of the following best approximates the density of the planetoid, in grams per cubic centimeter?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98079,"html":"<p>3.6</p>","correct":false},{"id":98080,"html":"<p>4.1</p>","correct":false},{"id":98081,"html":"<p>4.6</p>","correct":true},{"id":98082,"html":"<p>5.5</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26508,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/2JuwGezPiHy5SCLqprYU2yj9niEF9eKHYAnYZPKC.png\" style=\"width: 311.421px; height: 302.179px;\"></div><br>Twelve data points are shown in the scatterplot. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. At x = 1,200, which of the following is closest to the y-value predicted by the line of best fit?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98083,"html":"<p>16</p>","correct":false},{"id":98084,"html":"<p>14</p>","correct":false},{"id":98085,"html":"<p>11</p>","correct":true},{"id":98086,"html":"<p>6</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26509,"html":"<p>The scatterplot shows the relationship between the weight, in pounds, of each of 9 female gray wolves on April 30 and the number of offspring each gray wolf produced.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/MOukZIfzOaHjY82PRxQXpeoT8Ylq1REp4Ivcuyvc.png\" style=\"width: 345.257px; height: 325.159px;\"><br></div><br>How many offspring did the 50-pound gray wolf produce?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98087,"html":"<p>8</p>","correct":false},{"id":98088,"html":"<p>7</p>","correct":false},{"id":98089,"html":"<p>6</p>","correct":true},{"id":98090,"html":"<p>5</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26510,"html":"<p>The table shows selected values from function f.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/iCJ22YYqlb8NxrbOjbuTQn5uvo5UzS186AUL8IdK.png\" style=\"width: 175.966px;\"><br></div><br>Which of the following is the best description of function f?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98091,"html":"<p>Decreasing linear</p>","correct":false},{"id":98092,"html":"<p>Increasing linear</p>","correct":true},{"id":98093,"html":"<p>Decreasing exponential</p>","correct":false},{"id":98094,"html":"<p>Increasing exponential</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26511,"html":"<p>The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, x and y.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/GdVfVHC4LVIvnOIIozS6pMO8wiE4xXYK7zNc1G2B.png\" style=\"width: 317.628px; height: 290.114px;\"></div><br>Which of the following graphs shows the most appropriate model for the data?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98095,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/tgHM9NqWQbJ15fO5y7TKAySjBlDhWn4i05gOBNMu.png\" style=\"width: 360.98px;\"><br></p>","correct":false},{"id":98096,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/MBJ7qHOBysPrrtDfr7jVQbMt6LOa26m6g6P1legc.png\" style=\"width: 354.986px;\"><br></p>","correct":true},{"id":98097,"html":"<p>-</p>","correct":false},{"id":98098,"html":"<p>-</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26512,"html":"<p>The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, x and y. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. Which of the following is closest to the difference between the y-coordinate of the data point with x = 1 and the y-value predicted by the line of best fit at x = 1?<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/8D2jsXsHv4K7oyMOvc7Si1CqUDZfHLblqLFWejnP.png\" style=\"width: 232.4px; height: 235.702px;\"></div><p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98099,"html":"<p>1</p>","correct":true},{"id":98100,"html":"<p>2</p>","correct":false},{"id":98101,"html":"<p>5</p>","correct":false},{"id":98102,"html":"<p>12</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26513,"html":"<p>In the given scatterplot, a line of best fit for the data is shown.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/ITdlsqaB2QQtZ3ugd6x9ZO5cwk5E2jMn8264zq5K.png\" style=\"width: 292.125px; height: 285.712px;\"><br></div><br>Which of the following is closest to the slope of this line of best fit?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98103,"html":"<p>7</p>","correct":false},{"id":98104,"html":"<p>0.7</p>","correct":false},{"id":98105,"html":"<p>-0.7</p>","correct":true},{"id":98106,"html":"<p>-7</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26514,"html":"<p>Which of the following is true about the values of 2x and 2x + 2 for x &gt; 0?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98107,"html":"<p>For all x &gt; 0, it is true that 2x &lt; 2x + 2.</p>","correct":false},{"id":98108,"html":"<p>For all x &gt; 0, it is true that 2x &gt; 2x + 2.</p>","correct":false},{"id":98109,"html":"<p>There is a constant c such that if 0 &lt; x &lt; c, then 2x &lt; 2x + 2, but if x &gt; c, then 2x &gt; 2x + 2</p>","correct":true},{"id":98110,"html":"<p>There is a constant c such that if 0 &lt; x &lt; c, then 2x &gt; 2x + 2, but if x &gt; c, then 2x &lt; 2x + 2</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26515,"html":"<p>The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, x and y. A line of best fit is also shown.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/bPaACvTeKUcKA3CngVoJAQgnObT463b6wBpo8wlw.png\" style=\"width: 301.636px; height: 297.86px;\"></div><br>Which of the following is closest to the slope of the line of best fit shown?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98111,"html":"<p>-2.4</p>","correct":false},{"id":98112,"html":"<p>-0.8</p>","correct":true},{"id":98113,"html":"<p>0.8</p>","correct":false},{"id":98114,"html":"<p>2.4</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26516,"html":"<p>An inspector begins a day of work with a large sample of shirts that need to be checked for defects. The inspector works at a constant rate throughout the morning. What type of model is best to model the number of shirts remaining to be checked for defects at any given time throughout the morning?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98115,"html":"<p>A linear model with a positive slope</p>","correct":false},{"id":98116,"html":"<p>A linear model with a negative slope</p>","correct":true},{"id":98117,"html":"<p>An exponential growth model</p>","correct":false},{"id":98118,"html":"<p>An exponential decay model</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26517,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/ngaPhfiPhpJmSHsJWg2K2nC451D4O2SgwMRSbLrZ.png\" style=\"width: 334.972px;\"></div><br>The scatterplot above shows data for ten charities along with the line of best fit. For the charity with the greatest percent of total expenses spent on programs, which of the following is closest to the difference of the actual percent and the percent predicted by the line of best fit?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98119,"html":"<p>10%</p>","correct":false},{"id":98120,"html":"<p>7%</p>","correct":true},{"id":98121,"html":"<p>4%</p>","correct":false},{"id":98122,"html":"<p>1%</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26518,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/YEQ4iRxQVqr7tgdH8mUBizf83iwDGDZVUqbWLsd1.png\" style=\"width: 253.636px; height: 275.825px;\"></div><br>Teach dot in the scatterplot above represents the height x, in feet, in the high jump, and the distance y, in feet, in the long jump, made by each student in a group of twenty students. The graph of which of the following equations is a line that most closely fits the data?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98123,"html":"<p>y = 0.82x + 3.30</p>","correct":false},{"id":98124,"html":"<p>y = 0.82x - 0.82</p>","correct":false},{"id":98125,"html":"<p>y = 3.30x + 0.82</p>","correct":true},{"id":98126,"html":"<p>y = 3.30x - 3.30</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26519,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/z67VXKnhO2xTzCkzZhstaI9OrrNeYvuNEsxaUXrE.png\" style=\"width: 314.125px; height: 241.846px;\"></div><br>The scatterplot above shows the number of visitors to a railroad museum in Pennsylvania each year from 1968 to 1980, where t is the number of years since 1968 and n is the number of visitors. A line of best fit is also shown. Which of the following could be an equation of the line of best fit shown?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98127,"html":"<p>n = 16,090 + 4,680t</p>","correct":true},{"id":98128,"html":"<p>n = 4,690 + 16,090t</p>","correct":false},{"id":98129,"html":"<p>n = 16,090 + 9,060t</p>","correct":false},{"id":98130,"html":"<p>n = 9,060 + 16,090t</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26520,"html":"<p>In which of the following tables is the relationship between the values of x and their corresponding y-values nonlinear?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98131,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/tKyKEDqAHlC3MRdxsBUlv9GVBaSHdpBpt9KDwbI1.png\" style=\"width: 242.983px;\"><br></p>","correct":false},{"id":98132,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/sCRXBXQsk4oXjqT8V5F9gUOVNPGJHNYm57CED8Md.png\" style=\"width: 240.98px;\"><br></p>","correct":false},{"id":98133,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/mwkRFevGAp7QECJZrJB4hLRar8Tn9JxMIvXgXzl4.png\" style=\"width: 235.98px;\"><br></p>","correct":false},{"id":98134,"html":"<p><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/JZ1VGV4pwsnqvyeIcZSAajY7zEbOf7sizlDGbVoL.png\" style=\"width: 240.98px;\"><br></p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26521,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/VZ5tk00NVkozru4UcNtXlMXCqDhQ42IBnjqo3oBA.png\" style=\"width: 262.635px; height: 194.312px;\"></div><br>Which of the following could be the equation for a line of best fit for the data shown in the scatterplot above?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98135,"html":"<p>y = 3x + 0.8</p>","correct":true},{"id":98136,"html":"<p>y = 0.8x + 3</p>","correct":false},{"id":98137,"html":"<p>y = -0.8x + 3</p>","correct":false},{"id":98138,"html":"<p>y = -3x + 0.8</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26522,"html":"<p>The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, x and y. A line of best fit for the data is also shown.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/ZJQnzzdSoibd6I8uwR9OxvuGMorwkvHFsFrsLTzC.png\" style=\"width: 305px;\"></div><br>At x = 32, which of the following is closest to the y-value predicted by the line of best fit?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98139,"html":"<p>0.4</p>","correct":false},{"id":98140,"html":"<p>1.5</p>","correct":false},{"id":98141,"html":"<p>2.4</p>","correct":true},{"id":98142,"html":"<p>3.3</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26523,"html":"<p>In the given scatterplot, a line of best fit for the data is shown.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/XMPUXmFvOb8f0mw90NV73oOms29mezE89WAVItHn.png\" style=\"width: 281.625px; height: 278.248px;\"></div><br>Which of the following is closest to the slope of the line of best fit shown?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98143,"html":"<p>0.2</p>","correct":false},{"id":98144,"html":"<p>0.7</p>","correct":false},{"id":98145,"html":"<p>1.8</p>","correct":true},{"id":98146,"html":"<p>2.6</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26524,"html":"<p>The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, x and y. A line of best fit for the data is also shown.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/OFIgdRyGENeeBRmp9bKm4jARX5HNCESWd0H8qaWg.png\" style=\"width: 305.522px; height: 301.812px;\"></div><br>For how many of the 10 data points is the actual y-value greater than the y-value predicted by the line of best fit?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98147,"html":"<p>3</p>","correct":false},{"id":98148,"html":"<p>4</p>","correct":false},{"id":98149,"html":"<p>6</p>","correct":true},{"id":98150,"html":"<p>7</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26525,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/mgQG23qLPtsqg0twp0LeylngrmkrJXrpyZZWI4v0.png\" style=\"width: 324.119px; height: 266.793px;\"></div><br>The scatterplot above shows the federal-mandated minimum wage every 10 years between 1940 and 2010. A line of best fit is shown, and its equation is y = 0.096x - 0.488. What does the line of best fit predict about the increase in the minimum wage over the 70-year period?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98151,"html":"<p>Each year between 1940 and 2010, the average increase in minimum wage was 0.096 dollars.</p>","correct":true},{"id":98152,"html":"<p>Each year between 1940 and 2010, the average increase in minimum wage was 0.49 dollars.</p>","correct":false},{"id":98153,"html":"<p>Every 10 years between 1940 and 2010, the average increase in minimum wage was 0.096 dollars.</p>","correct":false},{"id":98154,"html":"<p>Every 10 years between 1940 and 2010, the average increase in minimum wage was 0.488 dollars.</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26526,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/p8QUGumE8jDYjwWz3aAucWaubjSm2zBE0S88thm8.png\" style=\"width: 374.119px; height: 249.099px;\"></div><br>The scatterplot above shows a company’s ice cream sales d, in dollars, and the high temperature t, in degrees Celsius (0C), on 12 different days. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. Which of the following could be an equation of the line of best fit?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98155,"html":"<p>d = 0.03t + 402</p>","correct":false},{"id":98156,"html":"<p>d = 10t + 402</p>","correct":false},{"id":98157,"html":"<p>d = 33t + 300</p>","correct":false},{"id":98158,"html":"<p>d = 33t + 84</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26527,"html":"<p>The scatterplot below shows the amount of electric energy generated, in millions of megawatt-hours, by nuclear sources over a 10-year period.<br></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/00rftyDgJUb6tT0HTVjGTLb0maVhU8jQZFGjRttW.png\" style=\"width: 334.986px;\"></div><br>Of the following equations, which best models the data in the scatterplot?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":98159,"html":"<p>y = 1.674x<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> - 745.73</p>","correct":false},{"id":98160,"html":"<p>y = 1.674x<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">^2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></sp